In the GoogleAdsRow, all getters have their own return type. However, they are `null` by default, and will return `null` if they're not set.

**Example**:
```
/**
 * The campaign referenced in the query.
 *
 * Generated from protobuf field <code>.google.ads.googleads.v6.resources.Campaign campaign = 2;</code>
 * @return \Google\Ads\GoogleAds\V6\Resources\Campaign
 */
public function getCampaign()
{
    return isset($this->campaign) ? $this->campaign : null;
}
```

Which should be;
```
/**
 * The campaign referenced in the query.
 *
 * Generated from protobuf field <code>.google.ads.googleads.v6.resources.Campaign campaign = 2;</code>
 * @return \Google\Ads\GoogleAds\V6\Resources\Campaign|null
 */
public function getCampaign()
{
    return isset($this->campaign) ? $this->campaign : null;
}
```

Right now, PHPStan will fail on checking if these return `null`, because the return type doesn't include it.

class TestAcme2Controller extends ZControlCmd
{

    public function file_force_contents( $fullPath, $contents, $flags = 0 ){
        $parts = explode( '/', $fullPath );
        array_pop( $parts );
        $dir = implode( '/', $parts );

        if( !is_dir( $dir ) )
            mkdir( $dir, 0777, true );

        file_put_contents( $fullPath, $contents, $flags );
    }

    public function actionRun()
    {
        //Prepare flysystem
        $adapter = new Local('data');

        $filesystem = new Filesystem($adapter);

        //Construct the client
        $client = new Client([
            'username' => 'jobiryusupov0@gmail.com',
            'fs'       => $filesystem,
            'mode'     => Client::MODE_STAGING,
        ]);

        $order = $client->createOrder(['vadeacme.zoft.uz']);

        $authorizations = $client->authorize($order);

